; REDUNDANCY UNSOUNDNESS.  Same program as 35 with one slot literal changed
; (here (Var 0), there (Var 9)); the two must agree, and neither may collapse
; the variable class.
;
; Nothing here says $5 and $6 are interchangeable, so k($5) and k($6) must stay
; apart.  slotted-egraphs agrees for both slot choices (the rule never matches
; there -- revisiting a redundant slot allocates a fresh one).
;
; Today: this file collapses every variable into one, 35 does not.
; The match that causes it uses a candidate symmetry triple that only exists
; mid-repair: the final e-graph contains no row that satisfies the rule's guard,
; and the stored node is (App2 "sub" (map-of 0 0) ...) here but
; (App2 "sub" (map-of 0 9) ...) in 35 -- a redundant slot keeps whatever name it
; happened to have instead of being renamed to $0 as Def. 7 requires.

(rewrite
    (App2 "f" (App2 "sub" x x) (App2 "sub" x x))
    x
)

(let $s (App2 "sub" (Var 0) (Var 0)))
(let $z (Null))
(union $s $z)

(let $w (App2 "f" (App2 "sub" (Var 0) (Var 0)) (App2 "sub" (Var 1) (Var 1))))

(let $k5 (App2 "k" (Var 5) (Null)))
(let $k6 (App2 "k" (Var 6) (Null)))

(run 20)

(fail (check (= $k5 $k6)))
